# CODEOWNERS
#
# Defines who must review changes to specific paths.
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner(s)>
#
# GitHub docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# --- Docs / context layer ---
# Tech Lead must review any changes to the AI context docs and system prompts.
# These files directly affect the quality of all AI-generated output.
docs/context/                   @tech-lead
docs/schemas/                   @tech-lead

# --- PRDs ---
# Product Owner owns all product requirement documents (live on prd branch).
docs/prd/                       @product-owner

# --- Roadmap / milestones ---
# Project Manager owns milestone files.
docs/roadmap/                   @project-manager

# --- AI pipeline scripts ---
# Tech Lead must review changes to the scripts that call Claude and interact with GitHub.
.claude/scripts/                @tech-lead

# --- GitHub Actions workflows ---
# Tech Lead must review workflow changes (security-sensitive).
.github/workflows/              @tech-lead

# --- Backend ---
# Any engineer can review backend changes; no single owner enforced.
# Add a specific handle here if you want a mandatory reviewer:
# backend/                      @backend-lead

# --- Frontend ---
# frontend/                     @frontend-lead

# --- AI-generated PRs ---
# PRs labeled `ai-generated` are reviewed by humans — no bot account needed.
# The ai-code-review.yml workflow posts an automated review as a first pass,
# but a human must approve before merge (enforced by branch protection on dev).
